From b1c0f904390177aec9530c3bd25969fb99bdb31f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Medium1992 <Medium1992@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 03:33:01 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] XHTTP: Keep the flow governor's send window total as
 counters, let the guard lift it

downRelease walked every stream of the connection for each stream it looked
at, so one SETTINGS frame cost the square of the open streams, on a path an
unauthenticated client reaches. What the client holds is now kept as three
counters that change with the streams.

A client that returns credit only once half of its window is read never got
that half at the limit, and the guard handed out nothing: the downloads
stopped for good. The guard now lifts the limit on a connection whose client
has returned nothing in small steps.

The limit covers the streams the server has not finished; the comments said
"in all". The clock skip in the PING check is taken out again: it had no
measurement of its own, and it let a PING that was due wait.
